 are satisfied. The restart protocol is coherent: node1 was running before restart with boot ID 9bdcc129-3d25-48ff-ad64-56be332fb91e, acknowledged a scheduled reboot, briefly reset the connection, returned running with boot ID 4a81e8f9-24aa-4a14-97c8-4edb510dc9c9, and retained the policy and enforcement behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the identity change.","limitations":["Behavior was tested through pwscore with PAM integration verified from configuration, rather than through an end-to-end password change using passwd. This is strong but slightly less direct evidence of the complete user-password workflow.","No separate application data or cluster recovery probe was applicable to this single standalone node; recovery evidence covers system state, root filesystem availability, PAM configuration, password-policy behavior, and baseline listening services."]}
